<article class="env-lemma" id="0F52">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F52">Lemma <span data-tag="0F52">63.3.6</span>.</a> Let $Y$ be a scheme. Let $j : X \to \overline{X}$ be an open immersion of schemes over $Y$ with $\overline{X}$ proper over $Y$. Denote $f : X \to Y$ and $\overline{f} : \overline{X} \to Y$ the structure morphisms. For $\mathcal{F} \in \textit{Ab}(X_{\acute{e}tale})$ there is a canonical isomorphism (see proof) </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f_!\mathcal{F} \longrightarrow \overline{f}_!j_!\mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
  <p> As we have $\overline{f}_! = \overline{f}_*$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F51" data-tag="0F51">63.3.4</a> we obtain $\overline{f}_* \circ j_! = f_!$ as functors $\textit{Ab}(X_{\acute{e}tale}) \to \textit{Ab}(Y_{\acute{e}tale})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have $(j_!\mathcal{F})|_ X = \mathcal{F}$, see Étale Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0F70" data-tag="0F70">59.70.4</a>. Thus the displayed arrow is the injective map $f_!(\mathcal{G}|_ X) \to \overline{f}_!\mathcal{G}$ of Remark <a href="/tag/0F53" data-tag="0F53">63.3.5</a> for $\mathcal{G} = j_!\mathcal{F}$. The explicit nature of this map implies that it now suffices to show: if $V \in Y_{\acute{e}tale}$ and $s \in \overline{f}_!\mathcal{G}(V) = \overline{f}_*\mathcal{G}(V) = \mathcal{G}(\overline{X}_ V)$ is a section, then the support of $s$ is contained in the open $X_ V \subset \overline{X}_ V$. This is immediate from the fact that the stalks of $\mathcal{G}$ are zero at geometric points of $\overline{X} \setminus X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>